n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786815200799\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Running the newbound SERVER in a disposable (2026-08-16): http only comes up if runtime/<app>/app.properties exists for EVERY app in config.properties apps= (stage each from data/<lib>/_APPS/<app>/) - init_globals loads libraries and registers the boot timers (incl app:service:init which binds HTTP) from those files; missing = silent no-listener. Also set http_port to a real port (0 = disabled). At boot the server auto-logs-in admin and prints http://localhost:<port>/<app>/index.html?sessionid=... to stdout - use that session for browser automation (admin password persists in users/admin.properties). curl needs --noproxy in the container.\",\n    \"tags\": \"testing\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786899133310\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Disposable-testing gotcha (cost an hour, 2026-08-17): a command upserted via dev.code in an MCP session is compiled into the dylib on disk but NOT loaded into that same process - hot reload only runs in server mode. Calling it in the same session yields No-such-command (and paths that swallow errors, like the executives catch_unwind around ask_llm, go silently dead - escalations read 0 with no error anywhere). Batteries must upsert stubs in one MCP session, kill it, and run assertions in a FRESH session.\",\n    \"tags\": \"testing\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786973023250\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"upsert_command has no desc parameter: a new command compiles and is callable immediately but stays INVISIBLE to tools/list until set_command_meta fills its desc - authoring and publishing to discovery are two separate steps\",\n    \"detail\": \"Bit during H1: all three agent.msg commands worked but --list showed nothing until their descs were set. desc is also the curation lever for what the model sees.\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,desc,discovery\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1787139770609