laim\": \"dev.code.set_groups derives the ENFORCED readers arrays from the groups string at save time, at all three levels: library meta.json; control record plus its inline data records (app.read's gate); command META record (the array check_security reads via lookup_command_id) plus impl record. Empty groups derives [] = admin-only. Returns changed/groups/readers.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Restores the retired editcontrol/editcommand derivation (readers = groups.split(',')). Library-level readers refresh into system.libraries on restart. writers is never touched (only app.delete consults it).\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,set_groups,readers,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390464\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"patch_command_body, set_command_imports, and upsert_command preserve existing readers/writers on the records they rewrite; before 2026-08-09 every code edit reset a gated command to admin-only, because flowlang's data::write::write stamps whatever arrays it is passed.\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,readers,dev.code,preservation\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390468\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The 17 author-taking dev.code commands declare nn_sessionid (platform-injected on all web calls) and default an empty author to the session user; set_module_flag no longer exists.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Browser clients pass author:\\\"\\\" — journals record the real session displayname. CLI/MCP callers pass author explicitly (provenance names like \\\"claude\\\") AND nn_sessionid:\\\"\\\" — every declared param required. The builder does not garbage-collect deleted commands: prune the generated .rs and its mod.rs registration by hand after delete_command on a static lib. Clean generated-src commits come from a de-overlay + newbound rebuild + re-overlay cycle (the de-overlayed binary loses the agent commands until re-regenerated — rebuild again after re-overlaying before any archivist call); the regenerated initializer may drop the cmd-scaffold block when data/cmd is absent — restore it rather than committing that noise.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786406673052\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.set_timer fails under `newbound exec` (add_timer needs the `system` globals that only init_globals creates) - run it through `newbound mcp` instead.\",\n    \"detail\": \"The failure is late: the timer component record and the control's timer entry are already written when add_timer panics, and the _patches journal entry is skipped. Re-running the same set_timer over mcp replaces the record and journals normally (replace-only semantics heal the partial write). Observed 2026-08-11 wiring dev.code.init.\",\n    \"tags\": \"set_timer, exec, mcp, globals\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786419691108\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.init (boot timer, start 0, once) seeds runtime/metaidentity with the default identity \\\"Some Dev\\\" when the record is absent, so fresh clones publish without hand-seeding.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Same pattern as security.security.init: an init timer on the dev.code control. No-op when an identity exists; edit via the workbench publish pane or dev.code.set_meta_identity. Landed on branch claude/metaidentity-startup-init-euh44x (newbound 6018c09); the scratch-instance recipes no longer seed by hand. Timers only fire under `newbound` (run mode) - exec and mcp modes never start timer_loop.\",\n    \"tags\": \"metaidentity, publishapp, boot, dev.code\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786419738826\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Library static assets pattern (owner idiom): plain files under data/<lib>/_ASSETS/ may be placed directly (the no-hand-edit rule covers store records, not _ASSETS) and compiled into command dylibs via include_str with a ../../../../data/<lib>/_ASSETS/... relative path - resolves correctly through both the overlay symlink and the real checkout. system_call (flowlang::flowlang::system::system_call) runs bash -c strings; nohup ... & inside detaches services cleanly.\",\n    \"tags\": \"assets\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786840042173\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Dylib-authoring gotcha: a command upserted mid-session is invisible to the ALREADY-RUNNING process that authored it - Command::lookup resolves against the dylib loaded at startup, so calling a just-authored command requires a fresh process. Author first, then start the process that exercises it.\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase3,gotcha\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786815200799\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Running the newbound SERVER in a disposable (2026-08-16): http only comes up if runtime/<app>/app.properties exists for EVERY app in config.properties apps= (stage each from data/<lib>/_APPS/<app>/) - init_globals loads libraries and registers the boot timers (incl app:service:init which binds HTTP) from those files; missing = silent no-listener. Also set http_port to a real port (0 = disabled). At boot the server auto-logs-in admin and prints http://localhost:<port>/<app>/index.html?sessionid=... to stdout - use that session for browser automation (admin password persists in users/admin.properties). curl needs --noproxy in the container.\",\n    \"tags\": \"testing\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786899133310\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Disposable-testing gotcha (cost an hour, 2026-08-17): a command upserted via dev.code in an MCP session is compiled into the dylib on disk but NOT loaded into that same process - hot reload only runs in server mode. Calling it in the same session yields No-such-command (and paths that swallow errors, like the executives catch_unwind around ask_llm, go silently dead - escalations read 0 with no error anywhere). Batteries must upsert stubs in one MCP session, kill it, and run assertions in a FRESH session.\",\n    \"tags\": \"testing\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786973023250\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"upsert_command has no desc parameter: a new command compiles and is callable immediately but stays INVISIBLE to tools/list until set_command_meta fills its desc - authoring and publishing to discovery are two separate steps\",\n    \"detail\": \"Bit during H1: all three agent.msg commands worked but --list showed nothing until their descs were set. desc is also the curation lever for what the model sees.\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,desc,discovery\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1787139770609\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Content-addressed storage is a CHOICE the store permits, not a property it has: set_data shards purely by id (flowlang datastore.rs get_data_file), ids are system-minted unless the caller supplies one, and supplying id = hash-of-content gives structural dedup (owner, 2026-08-19). Hash a whole record and nothing ever dedupes - split content (id=hash of text) from occurrence (minted or chained id) when occurrences carry their own facts\",\n    \"detail\": \"agent.msg is the working example: mc<fnv128-of-text> content records, mo... occurrence records pointing at them. Two speakers saying the same word = one content record, two occurrences.\",\n    \"tags\": \"datastore,content-addressing,dedup\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1787139770694\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Facets are ATTACHMENTS: a control record's data carries attachmentkeynames and the content lives in sibling files (<id>.js etc.); get_data resolves them into data on read (both serde and non-serde paths), so d.has(facet)/get_string(facet) work after get_data - but raw record JSON on disk does NOT contain facet text\",\n    \"tags\": \"datastore,facets,attachments\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1787140461633\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev-code-evaluate_rust cannot work through per-call `newbound mcp` processes: it waits for hot reload, which only runs in server mode. The fresh-process driver's equivalent: upsert a scratch command in one call, execute it in the next (each nb-call IS a fresh process, so the same-session dylib gotcha never bites), delete it and prune the generated rs after\",\n    \"tags\": \"evaluate_rust,scratch,testing\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1787140461927\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"CORRECTION (2026-08-19, five-run instrumented investigation): the same-session dylib gotcha's MECHANISM was misdiagnosed - the hot-reload watcher IS armed under `newbound mcp` (initialize_all_commands starts it before the subcommand dispatch; its startup banner and inotify watches confirmed by strace). What actually fails is the reload-register seam: on a new-command upsert the watcher detects the change and dlopens the fresh temp copy, yet the command never appears in RUST_COMMANDS (5/5 reproductions, 15-25s waits), and in one run the debouncer thread died mid-println with no panic message. Related known bug (owner): hot-swapping while code from that same library runs in another thread crashes the whole process in server mode. The FACT stands - a command upserted in a live process is not callable in that process - but for new commands in EXISTING libraries too, not only new crates, and not because the watcher is absent\",\n    \"detail\": \"Consequences unchanged: author in one process, execute in a fresh one (each nb-call IS a fresh process, so the driver idiom is naturally safe); evaluate_rust cannot succeed in ANY single mcp process until the reload-register seam is fixed. interim-process.md section 2 claims this path verified working 2026-08-09 (flowlang 0.3.31 era) - either it regressed by 0.3.33 or that verification measured something else; worth an owner look at FlowLangLibrary::reload (call_mirror's Result is silently discarded - a diagnosability fix regardless). Also: every process start copies each dylib to /tmp/lib<name>_<ts>.so and cleanup rides Drop, so kill/terminate leaks them - 142 accumulated in one session of fresh-process calls.\",\n    \"tags\": \"hot-reload,mcp,dylib,gotcha\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1787141356049\n  }\n]\n","old":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"list_control_patches returns newest-FIRST — two probe harnesses have failed by reading the wrong end\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,journal\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"/app/read answers 500 for the runtime library (store-only, never app-loaded) — read runtime state through dedicated commands (get_meta_identity, dev.plugins.list_plugins)\",\n    \"tags\": \"runtime,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.3\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"groups is SECURITY groups; categorization lives in the tags field via set_tags — never write tags into groups\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,tags,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.8\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"New dev.code commands are upsert → cargo build → restart (no dylib). Agent-lib commands keep the dylib hot-swap, which can abort mid-request over HTTP — author those over MCP\",\n    \"tags\": \"dev.code,upsert_command,mcp\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"CONTRACT.md §6.6\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785504820517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.set_groups derives the ENFORCED readers arrays from the groups string at save time, at all three levels: library meta.json; control record plus its inline data records